<title>LUXEMBOURG: Court annuls in part Commission decision to reduce funds.</title>
<headline>Court annuls in part Commission decision to reduce funds.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Court of First Instance annulled in part the European Commission's decision to reduce monies for a training programme in Portugal.</p>
<p>The court dismissed most of the appeal, rejecting arguments that the Commission violated principles of protection of acquired interests, legal certainty, and legitimate expectations when it reduced approved funds for a hotel training programme from 60 million escudos to 42 million escudos.</p>
<p>However, the court annulled the part of the Commission decision which reduced funds strictly because costs corresponding to the programme had not been approved in the original agreement.</p>
<p>***</p>
